==Strategy==
When playing this stage, you will likely not have any trouble at all due to just how trivial this stage is.

Malevolent Eraser carries the highest health stat for a non-collab unit, however his damage is lowered in return for a guaranteed chance to create a level 2 surge. Because of this surge, units that are [[Immune to Surge|Surge Immune]] are very much necessary here. One of the best examples here is a [[Talents|talented]] [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon]], who can deal big damage once stacked. Good meatshield options include [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone]] (as always) and [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cactus]], who is Surge Immune and is pretty tanky against Akus.

With a way to stall and kill the boss, it's time to think about the peon waves. The first wave is a duo of LeMurrs, which will be the most difficult wave for most. The two LeMurrs are single target, but boast incredibly high DPS in exchange, and can melt through your defenses if you're not ready. However, bringing specific trait counters isn't necessary. As long as you're meatshielding, your ranged attackers should be able to take care of them. The Angelic Gories are ''meant'' to be the main pushers, but if you bring [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen]], then they shouldn't pose a threat. At all. The singular Zir Zeal will only be a threat if you allow it to burrow, but if you bring Breakerblast and interrupt his burrow, he is literally nothing. The Haniwanwans are just filler enemies, and if you brought a unit like [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]], they are just free cash. Speaking of free cash, Mistress Celeboodles spawn periodically, so you'll never run out.

All in all, a very simple stage and shouldn't be a threat if you are prepared.

